  {
   "t": "<b>Same gene, different variant.</b> Carbamazepine goes with HLA-B*15:02 and a skin reaction (SJS/TEN); abacavir goes with HLA-B*57:01 and a whole-organ hypersensitivity reaction. A negative test for one variant does not clear the other drug.",
   "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 280\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Carbamazepine with HLA-B 15:02 and abacavir with HLA-B 57:01: same gene, different variant.\"><text x=\"180\" y=\"20\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-weight:600;font-size:14px\">Ziagen (abacavir) label</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"36\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"middle\">her worksheet: eight questions per label</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"60\" width=\"156\" height=\"120\" rx=\"6\" class=\"s3box\"/><rect x=\"190\" y=\"60\" width=\"156\" height=\"120\" rx=\"6\" class=\"s3hi\"/><text x=\"92\" y=\"88\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-weight:600\">Carbamazepine</text><text x=\"92\" y=\"118\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:15px\">HLA-B*15:02</text><text x=\"92\" y=\"150\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"middle\">skin: SJS / TEN</text><text x=\"268\" y=\"88\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-weight:600\">Abacavir</text><text x=\"268\" y=\"118\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:15px\">HLA-B*57:01</text><text x=\"268\" y=\"150\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"middle\">whole-organ reaction</text><line x1=\"92\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"268\" y2=\"196\" class=\"s3acc\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"216\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"middle\">same gene (HLA-B), different variant</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"246\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a negative test for one variant</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"262\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"middle\">does not clear the other drug</text></svg>",
   "say": "Her main point was the comparison with carbamazepine. She said, \"The H L A B gene is involved in both, but it's a different genetic variant for carbamazepine compared to abacavir, same gene.\" Carbamazepine goes with H L A B fifteen oh two. She said the carbamazepine reaction is in the skin, and the abacavir reaction is \"a whole organ hypersensitivity reaction.\" She said the abacavir problem was first identified as massive skin problems similar to carbamazepine. A negative test for one H L A B variant does not clear the other drug."
  }
