   "say": "This reading is the F D A prescribing information for Herceptin, which is trastuzumab, revised May twenty twenty six. It matters for Exam four because it is one of the three labels on Dr. Smith's Pharmacogenomics Questions worksheet, discussed on October twenty seventh. It is her example where the tumor is tested, not the patient, and where the test is about efficacy, not toxicity. The label calls Herceptin a Her two neu receptor antagonist. It is indicated in adults for Her two overexpressing breast cancer, and for Her two overexpressing metastatic gastric or gastroesophageal junction adenocarcinoma."
