   "t": "<b>6. Test named?</b> No brand kit; an FDA-authorized test",
   "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 324\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Herceptin (trastuzumab) label: her eight worksheet questions, answer 6 highlighted\"><text x=\"180\" y=\"20\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"font-weight:600;font-size:14px\">Herceptin (trastuzumab) label</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"36\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"middle\">her worksheet: eight questions per label</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"48\" width=\"344\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" class=\"s3box\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"67\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"start\">1 Gene and variant</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"61\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"start\" style=\"font-size:12px\">HER2 (185 kDa receptor);</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"74\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"start\" style=\"font-size:12px\">no variant named</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"82\" width=\"344\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" class=\"s3box\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"101\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"start\">2 What it does</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"95\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"start\" style=\"font-size:12px\">Blocks HER2-overexpressing</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"108\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"start\" style=\"font-size:12px\">tumor cells</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"116\" width=\"344\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" class=\"s3box\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"135\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"start\">3 Patient or tumor?</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"135\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"start\" style=\"font-size:12px\">The tumor (phenotyped)</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"150\" width=\"344\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" class=\"s3box\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"169\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"start\">4 Efficacy or toxicity?</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"169\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"start\" style=\"font-size:12px\">Ensure efficacy</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"184\" width=\"344\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" class=\"s3box\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"203\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"start\">5 How it is tested</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"197\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"start\" style=\"font-size:12px\">IHC on the tumor</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"210\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"start\" style=\"font-size:12px\">(trials also used FISH)</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"218\" width=\"344\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" class=\"s3hi\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"237\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"start\">6 Test named?</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"231\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"start\" style=\"font-size:12px\">No brand kit; an</text><text x=\"164\" y=\"244\" class=\"s3txt\" text-anchor=\"start\" style=\"font-size:12px\">FDA-authorized test</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"252\" width=\"344\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" class=\"s3box\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"271\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"start\">7 Who is tested</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"286\" width=\"344\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" class=\"s3box\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"305\" class=\"s3sub\" text-anchor=\"start\">8 What the result changes</text></svg>",
   "say": "Item six asks whether the F D A names a test. Dr. Smith said the label \"a few years ago used to name a certain brand of a kit.\" She said it no longer does, and that the test needs to be specific and sensitive. The current label names no brand. It asks for F D A authorized tests specific for breast or gastric cancers, done by laboratories with demonstrated proficiency."
